"Organization and Service Content | SHU-TE University Office of Student Affairs (https://en.sao.stu.edu.tw/organization/)\nciteturn318search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.9 years ago; Crawled: last month; ## Student Assistance Section ... Responsible for providing counseling, guidance, and program development related to students’ physical and mental health, and for coordinating affairs related to academic advisors and volunteer counseling teachers on campus.\n\n# Organization and Service Content\n\n## Student Assistance Section\n\nResponsible for matters related to student tuition reduction and exemption, student loans, scholarships and financial aid, leave applications, student safety education, military service affairs, international student services, and student housing applications.\n\nClick Here\n\n## Extracurricular Activities Section\n\nRegarding student clubs and equipment, the school anniversary celebration, campus fairs, and various off-campus student activities.\n\nClick Here\n\n## Student Wellness Center\n\nResponsible for providing counseling, guidance, and program development related to students’ physical and mental health, and for coordinating affairs related to academic advisors and volunteer counseling teachers on campus.\n\nClick Here\n\n## Campus Bullying Prevention Section\n\nThe Campus Bullying Prevention Section is responsible for promoting bullying prevention education, providing counseling and support resources, handling related reporting procedures, and fostering a safe and inclusive campus environment.\n\nClick Here\n\n## Gender Equality Education Committee\n\nResponsible for planning and promoting gender equality initiatives on campus, and for assisting in the investigation of related campus cases.\n\nClick Here\n\n## Counseling and Special Education Resource Center\n\nResponsible for providing support and guidance for students with special education needs in areas including daily life, mental health, academics, and career development, and for promoting matters related to creating an accessible campus environment.\n\nClick Here\n\n## Indigenous Students Resource Center\n\nResponsible for providing academic support and campus life guidance for Indigenous students, and for promoting Indigenous education initiatives across the campus.\n\nClick Here--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIntroduction | SHU-TE University Office of Student Affairs (https://en.sao.stu.edu.tw/introduction/)\nciteturn318search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.9 years ago; Crawled: last month;   * Providing assistance and services to students from overseas, and Mainland China, and in dorms ...   * Student Assistance Section ...   * Counseling and Special Education Resource Center\n\n# Introduction\n\nThis office adheres to the institutional motto, “Academics, Intellect, Happiness, and Hope” and also to “the diversified, integrated, open, and autonomous” spirit in order to promote comprehensive service to students.\n\nThe services of student affairs and consultation include:\n\n  * Implementation of settle-down schooling and campus safety\n  * Promoting community services, altruism, and innovation\n  * Providing assistance and services to students from overseas, and Mainland China, and in dorms\n  * Enhancing campus sanitation and all aspects of health\n  * Improving mental health and whole person development\n  * Promoting services and learning support for indigenous students\n  * Promoting sexual equality and friendly campus\n\nORGANIZATION\n\n  * Student Assistance Section\n  * Extracurricular Activities and Service Learning Section\n  * Overseas and Mainland Chinese Students and Housing Service Section\n  * Health Center\n  * Counseling and Special Education Resource Center\n  * Indigenous Students Resource Center\n  * Gender Equality Education Committee--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nINDEX | 樹德科技大學 教務處 (https://www.aca.stu.edu.tw/en/index-2/)\nciteturn318search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.8 years ago; Crawled: last month; It consists of Registration and Curriculum Division, Admissions and Selection Division,  which are in charge of student enrollment, and academic affairs pertinent to both students and teachers. ...   * Recruitment and admission affairs\n### 樹德科技大學 教務處\n\nSHU-TE UNIVERSITY Office of Academic Affairs\n\n[Input: Search]\n\n# INDEX\n\n# Office of Academic Affairs​\n\nThe Office of Academic Affairs provides academic services to all faculty and students. It consists of Registration and Curriculum Division, Admissions and Selection Division,  which are in charge of student enrollment, and academic affairs pertinent to both students and teachers. Pursuant to School Policy Purposes, Building a High-Quality Educational Services, Creating Effective Teaching and Learning Environments, Promote Holistic Teaching and Learning Development, In pursuit of a campus of “Academic, Intellectual, Happy, Hopeful”.\n\n## ORGANIZATION\n\nOffice of Academic Affairs\n\nDean of Academic Affairs\n\nTSAI, HSIN-YEH (ext: 2000) (Email: hsinyeh@stu.edu.tw)\n\nRegistration and Curriculum Division\n\n ◎Staff Members\n\n  * Division Chief\nCHOU, PEI-YI (ext2007) (E-mail: emma@stu.edu.tw )\n  * Assistant\nCHEN, YU-AN (ext:2009) (E-mail: etacojoy@stu.edu.tw)\n  * Project Assistant\nLin, Wen-Xuan (ext:2010) (E-mail: alice0517@stu.edu.tw)\n  * Officer\nTSAI, HSIN-LUN (ext:2012) (E-mail: perish@stu.edu.tw )\n  * Assistant\nHO, YING-TING (ext:2016) (E-mail: judy6820@stu.edu.tw )\n  * Officer\nCHENG, HSUEH-YU (ext:2014) (E-mail: beauty@stu.edu.tw )\n\n* * *\n\n◎Duties\n\n  * Registration service\n  * Entrance examinations\n  * Managing the application for study suspension, enrollment preservation, and related applications\n  * Managing the application for departmental transfer\n  * Issuing and reissuing student ID cards\n  * Recruitment and admission affairs\n  * Controlling the quotas of the undergraduate and graduate students\n  * Managing general curricular affairs\n  * Course arrangement\n  * Course selection\n  * Teaching evaluation\n  * Holding the meeting of Office of Academic Affairs\n  * Managing the application for minor and double major studies, and professional courses\n  * Managing the application for credits transfer\n  * Surveying the grades of graduating students\n  * Editing Journal of Shu-Te University\n  * Examining administrative plans\n  * Teaching Excellence Award\n  * Teaching Improvement Project & Award\n  * Information of academic publications\n\nAdmissions and Selection Division\n\n ◎Staff Members\n\n  * Division Chief\nTeng-Huang Huang (ext:2005) (E-mail: htime@stu.edu.tw )\n  * Deputy Leader\nHSU,CHUNG-WEI (ext:1905) (E-mail: waynehsu@stu.edu.tw )\n  * Officer\nWei-Ching Lee (ext:2004) (E-mail: weiching@stu.edu.tw )\n  * Officer\nChiung-Yi Yeh (ext:2015) (E-mail: iisayeh@stu.edu.tw )\n  * Officer\nSzu-Hui Lin (ext:2017) (E-mail: ariel@stu.edu.tw )\n  * Project  Assistant\nLI,HSIN-JU(ext:2021) (E-mail:lynn20180411@stu.edu.tw )\n  * Admissions Coordinator\nCHANG, YONG YING(ext:1902) (E-mail:cyy260515@stu.edu.tw )\n  * Admissions Coordinator\nCHEN,WEN-LING(ext:1904) (E-mail:wenling00@stu.edu.tw )\n\n◎Duties\n\n  * Works pertaining to the expansion of academic programs\n  * Entrance examinations\n  * Affairs pertaining to Pilot Scheme for the Professional Development of University Admissions, Ministry of Education\n  * All Admissions Outreach Efforts\n\n\n### 關於我們 | About Us\n\n  * 組織簡介｜Introduction\n  * 常見問答｜FAQs\n\n### 聯絡資訊 | Contact Us\n\n82445高雄市燕巢區橫山路59號行政大樓1樓\nNo.59, Hengshan Rd., Yanchao, Kaohsiung County 82445, Taiwan (R.O.C.)｜\n\nTel： +886-7-6158000 ext. list｜\nE-Mail： course@stu.edu.tw｜\nFax： (07)6158020｜\nOpening hours： Monday – Friday 8:00AM to 5:00PM--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n註冊課務組 | Registration and Curriculum Division | 樹德科技大學 教務處 (https://www.aca.stu.edu.tw/%E6%9C%8D%E5%8B%99%E5%B0